# Debian's kernels must never be installed by accident on b1nix. A dependency
# chain, a task metapackage or a dist-upgrade will otherwise try: plenty of
# packages depend on "linux-image" without caring which one, and b1nix-kernel
# provides that.
#
# This is a pin, not a conflict. Someone who deliberately wants Linux beside
# b1nix can still install it with `apt install -t ... linux-image-amd64`, and
# gets a second boot entry -- which is a useful escape hatch, not a bug.

Package: linux-image-* linux-headers-* linux-image-amd64 linux-image-arm64
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1
